 is the new industry standard. Every competitor reports BEAM scores. Scaling behavior is where graph memory should differentiate from flat vector stores."}]}],"id":"blk-70283","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70285","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101341","text":"Session 2: MemoryAgentBench"}]},{"id":"blk-70286","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101342","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101343","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101344","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8889e094cb2b904d65f6a29cd7861f1c"}]}],"id":"blk-70287","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70290","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101345","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101346","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.05257"}]}],"id":"blk-70289","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70292","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101347","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-101348","text":": https://github.com/HUST-AI-HYZ/MemoryAgentBench"}]}],"id":"blk-70291","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70294","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101349","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101350","text":": Multi-turn incremental format, includes EventQA and FactConsolidation"}]}],"id":"blk-70293","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70296","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101351","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101352","text":": 4 competency scores — accurate retrieval, test-time learning, long-range understanding, selective forgetting"}]}],"id":"blk-70295","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70298","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101353","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101354","text":": Multi-turn format requires simulating incremental store→query cycles, not batch ingest. Map \"selective forgetting\" to "},{"id":"spn-101355","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_by_policy"},{"id":"spn-101356","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-101357","marks":["code"],"text":"forget_node"},{"id":"spn-101358","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-70297","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70300","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101359","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101360","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101361","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench"}]}],"id":"blk-70299","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70302","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101362","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101363","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101364","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memoryagentbench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-70301","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70304","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101365","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why second"},{"id":"spn-101366","text":": Directly tests Graphonomous's differentiating features (forgetting, learning loop). ICLR 2026 paper — high credibility."}]}],"id":"blk-70303","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70305","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101367","text":"Session 3: LMEB (Long-horizon Memory Embedding Benchmark)"}]},{"id":"blk-70306","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70308","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101368","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101369","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101370","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_81c0f91f92b9b4a52e0a38b44c49a492"}]}],"id":"blk-70307","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70310","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101371","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101372","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12572"}]}],"id":"blk-70309","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70312","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101373","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repo"},{"id":"spn-101374","text":": https://github.com/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-70311","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70314","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101375","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-101376","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/KaLM-Embedding/LMEB"}]}],"id":"blk-70313","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70316","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101377","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101378","text":": 22 datasets, 193 zero-shot retrieval tasks across 4 memory types (episodic, dialogue, semantic, procedural)"}]}],"id":"blk-70315","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70318","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101379","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101380","text":": Retrieval accuracy per memory type, aggregate score"}]}],"id":"blk-70317","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70320","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101381","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101382","text":": This benchmarks the "},{"id":"spn-101383","marks":["italic"],"text":"embedding model"},{"id":"spn-101384","text":", not the full system. Run nomic-embed-text-v2-moe through the LMEB eval harness (likely Python). May need a thin Python wrapper or direct Elixir port of the eval logic."}]}],"id":"blk-70319","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70322","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101385","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101386","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101387","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb"}]}],"id":"blk-70321","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70324","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101388","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101389","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101390","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lmeb --model nomic-embed-text-v2-moe"}]}],"id":"blk-70323","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70326","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101391","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why third"},{"id":"spn-101392","text":": Cheapest to run (embedding-only, no LLM judge needed). Validates the foundational layer. If nomic scores poorly on memory-specific retrieval, that's a critical finding."}]}],"id":"blk-70325","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70327","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101393","text":"Session 4: MemoryBench (Continual Learning from Feedback)"}]},{"id":"blk-70328","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101394","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101395","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101396","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_8ef86ae124eb2f03375289107dcac5ae"}]}],"id":"blk-70329","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70332","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101397","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101398","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.17281"}]}],"id":"blk-70331","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101399","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101400","text":": User feedback simulation across multiple domains and languages"}]}],"id":"blk-70333","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101401","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101402","text":": Continual learning accuracy, feedback utilization rate, cross-domain transfer"}]}],"id":"blk-70335","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101403","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101404","text":": Requires simulating the feedback loop — "},{"id":"spn-101405","marks":["code"],"text":"learn_from_feedback"},{"id":"spn-101406","text":" with explicit/action-based/implicit feedback types, then re-querying to measure improvement. Multi-domain and multilingual means varied corpus."}]}],"id":"blk-70337","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101407","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101408","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101409","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench"}]}],"id":"blk-70339","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101410","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101411","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101412","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.memorybench --domain all --limit 100"}]}],"id":"blk-70341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101413","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fourth"},{"id":"spn-101414","text":": Directly tests the learning loop. Published finding that no system beats RAG baseline — if Graphonomous does, that's a headline result."}]}],"id":"blk-70343","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70345","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101415","text":"Session 5: LifeBench (Non-Declarative Memory)"}]},{"id":"blk-70346","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101416","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101417","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101418","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_824059ff9230ff0953646ea7ac2e7d6a"}]}],"id":"blk-70347","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101419","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101420","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.03781"}]}],"id":"blk-70349","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101421","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101422","text":": Long-horizon event simulations with real-world priors (surveys, maps, calendars)"}]}],"id":"blk-70351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101423","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101424","text":": Accuracy on habitual/procedural memory inference, declarative vs non-declarative breakdown"}]}],"id":"blk-70353","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101425","marks":["bold"],"text":"SOTA"},{"id":"spn-101426","text":": 55.2% (top system)"}]}],"id":"blk-70355","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101427","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101428","text":": Tests "},{"id":"spn-101429","marks":["italic"],"text":"inferred"},{"id":"spn-101430","text":" knowledge, not explicitly stored facts. Graphonomous procedural nodes + edge patterns may capture habitual patterns that flat stores miss. May need to extend "},{"id":"spn-101431","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_procedural"},{"id":"spn-101432","text":" or add inference logic."}]}],"id":"blk-70357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101433","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101434","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101435","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench"}]}],"id":"blk-70359","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101436","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101437","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101438","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.lifebench --limit 50"}]}],"id":"blk-70361","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101439","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why fifth"},{"id":"spn-101440","text":": Hardest benchmark (SOTA is 55%). Low expectations, high signal. If graph structure helps even marginally on non-declarative memory, that validates the architecture thesis."}]}],"id":"blk-70363","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70365","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101441","text":"Session 6: AMemGym (On-Policy Interactive)"}]},{"id":"blk-70366","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101442","marks":["bold"],"text":"Goal ID"},{"id":"spn-101443","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101444","marks":["code"],"text":"goal_b7ccffd9e67df8e7b42366ff24a9be82"}]}],"id":"blk-70367","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70370","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101445","marks":["bold"],"text":"Paper"},{"id":"spn-101446","text":": https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.01966"}]}],"id":"blk-70369","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101447","marks":["bold"],"text":"HuggingFace"},{"id":"spn-101448","text":": https://huggingface.co/datasets/AGI-Eval/AMemGym"}]}],"id":"blk-70371","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101449","marks":["bold"],"text":"Dataset"},{"id":"spn-101450","text":": Interactive on-policy benchmark — agent generates its own conversation"}]}],"id":"blk-70373","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101451","marks":["bold"],"text":"Metrics"},{"id":"spn-101452","text":": Structured state consistency, memory utilization, persona tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-70375","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101453","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key challenge"},{"id":"spn-101454","text":": This is fundamentally different from other benchmarks. The agent must "},{"id":"spn-101455","marks":["italic"],"text":"participate"},{"id":"spn-101456","text":" in the conversation, not just answer post-hoc questions. Requires wiring Graphonomous MCP into a simulated conversation loop with an LLM-simulated user. Most complex harness to build."}]}],"id":"blk-70377","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70380","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101457","marks":["bold"],"text":"Harness name"},{"id":"spn-101458","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101459","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym"}]}],"id":"blk-70379","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101460","marks":["bold"],"text":"CLI"},{"id":"spn-101461","text":": "},{"id":"spn-101462","marks":["code"],"text":"mix benchmark.amemgym --scenarios 10"}]}],"id":"blk-70381","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101463","marks":["bold"],"text":"Why last"},{"id":"spn-101464","text":": Most complex integration. Requires LLM-in-the-loop (simulated user). But the most realistic test of how Graphonomous actually performs in production. Save for last when all other harnesses are proven."}]}],"id":"blk-70383","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-70385","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101465","text":"Post-Completion"}]},{"id":"blk-70386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101466","text":"After all 6 harnesses are built and run:"}]},{"id":"blk-70387","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101467","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101468","marks":["code"],"text":"OS-E001-EMPIRICAL-EVALUATION.md"},{"id":"spn-101469","text":" with a unified results table"}]}],"id":"blk-70388","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70391","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101470","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101471","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous.com/benchmarks/"},{"id":"spn-101472","text":" pages with new benchmark results"}]}],"id":"blk-70390","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101473","text":"Update "},{"id":"spn-101474","marks":["code"],"text":"AmpersandBoxDesign/site/portfolio-review.html"},{"id":"spn-101475","text":" competitive landscape"}]}],"id":"blk-70392","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101476","text":"Store a comprehensive episodic node in Graphonomous summarizing the full evaluation"}]}],"id":"blk-70394","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70397","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101477","text":"Consider adding top-line scores to "},{"id":"spn-101478","marks":["code"],"text":"graphonomous/README.md"}]}],"id":"blk-70396","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-70398","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-101479","text":"Anti-Patterns to Avoid"}]},{"id":"blk-70399","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70401","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101480","text":"Do NOT modify "},{"id":"spn-101481","marks":["code"],"text":"retrieve_context"},{"id":"spn-101482","text":" or the retrieval pipeline to game a specific benchmark"}]}],"id":"blk-70400","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70403","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101483","text":"Do NOT add benchmark-specific code paths to the core engine"}]}],"id":"blk-70402","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101484","text":"Do NOT skip the smoke test ("},{"id":"spn-101485","marks":["code"],"text":"--limit 50"},{"id":"spn-101486","text":") before full runs"}]}],"id":"blk-70404","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101487","text":"Do NOT fabricate competitive baselines — only cite published numbers with sources"}]}],"id":"blk-70406","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-70409","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-101488","text":"Do NOT skip storing results in Graphonomous — the learning loop is the point"}]}],"id":"blk-70408","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierajkwlyx2ovm2qehb6ciq3ec7llcamu7wxvz26wdgsdxzdllf5ko4q","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}